	abstract = {E-petitions persist as one of the most popular, if controversial, forms of political participation online. E-petitions exist on a variety of platforms from government-run websites to charitable and commercial operations, each with different affordances. This chapter assesses these different affordances, drawing on research from across government and non-governmental e-petition platforms. The chapter identifies the key issues in current research on e-petitions and how findings cut across the different platforms. The chapter argues that e-petitions have the potential to impact policy and empower individuals, but this is shaped by how e-petitions are designed and institutionalized.},
